@startuml 04-deployment-flow
title Target Deployment Flow (what the SOPs will document)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #555555
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF3FA
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #6B8CB8
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FDF6EC

actor "Platform User" as U
participant "Git repo\n(from template)" as GIT
participant "CI Pipeline\n(tool selected in S1 ADR)" as CI
participant "Service Principal" as SP
participant "Databricks\ndev target" as DEV
participant "Databricks\nprod target" as PROD

== Develop ==
U -> GIT : branch + commit bundle changes
U -> U : local: bundle validate / deploy to dev sandbox

== Pull Request ==
U -> GIT : open PR
GIT -> CI : trigger
CI -> CI : databricks bundle validate
CI --> GIT : status check (required to merge)
U -> GIT : peer review + merge

== Deploy to dev ==
GIT -> CI : merge to main
CI -> SP : authenticate (OIDC)
SP -> DEV : bundle deploy --target dev
CI --> U : deployment result

== Promote to prod ==
U -> GIT : cut release tag
GIT -> CI : tag pipeline
CI -> CI : approval gate (manual)
CI -> SP : authenticate (prod SP)
SP -> PROD : bundle deploy --target prod
CI --> U : release recorded, rollback = redeploy prior tag
@enduml
